# J25 — Local monorepo baseline: entry + five-page current-state capture.
#
# Runs the production binary against the operator's existing local monorepo
# checkout (@TARGET via KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET — never a clone, copy, or
# fixture substitute) and records what every durable phase page currently
# shows before any new engagement work. This journey NEVER deletes or
# resets pre-existing `.kuzushi` engagement state on the target: prior
# findings, runs, and coverage rows are part of the baseline being recorded.
#
# The root-first whole-repository gate acceptance row lives in J29 (cycle 3), not
# here: this journey verifies harness truth on the real target — identity,
# non-destructive entry, honest page-state disclosure. Those facts can pass
# their machine checks, but the journey remains REVIEW REQUIRED until every
# `ask:` below receives an explicit human judgment.
name: Monorepo baseline · entry and phase pages (real target)
require-env: KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET
# When the scheduled audit pins a freshly-built native with
# KUZUSHI_NATIVE_BIN, the operator journey must still enter through `kz`.
require-wrapper-flow:
size: 120x36
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TARGET
wait-for: 60 KUZUSHI
# No setg here: the prompt can be owned by a launch-time run (G11/G17,
# cycle-3 ledger rows) and this journey's five-page capture works without
# it (proved at baseline). nav-mode converges Navigate regardless.
nav-mode:
keys: 1
wait-live-snap: 30 Viewing Map | map-initial
# Target identity must survive every size (top chrome renders `target ./<name>`):
expect: target ./
# Ready Map uses one compact target/revision/context receipt; readiness and
# partial-result cards own the expanded PROJECT CONTEXT label.
expect-wide: 80 context:
expect-wide: 80 rev:
ask: Map — with no accepted root scan baseline, is the single dominant NEXT action a root-level whole-repository scan, or does the page surface child-scope / non-root work without that gate?
ask: Map — are the repository facts on screen (target name, revision, scope names, counts) derived from the real checkout rather than hard-coded or fabricated?
keys: 2
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Scan | scan-initial
ask: Scan — are recorded receipts from the pre-existing engagement state clearly separated from live progress, and is scope-level scan guidance honestly gated when no root scan baseline exists?
keys: 3
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Review || Review is locked | review-initial
ask: Review — if findings exist, do they surface with honest run/revision provenance; otherwise, does the shell explicitly explain why Review is locked?
keys: Escape
nav-mode:
keys: 4
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Prove || Prove is locked | prove-initial
ask: Prove — if a confirmed finding exists, is its verification state honest; otherwise, does the shell explicitly explain why Prove is locked without fabricating proof?
keys: Escape
nav-mode:
keys: 5
wait-live-snap: 15 Viewing Fix || Fix is locked | fix-initial
ask: Fix — if proof or patch records exist, is remediation limited to planning/diff-preview with explicit application authorization; otherwise, does the shell explicitly explain why Fix is locked?
keys: Escape
